  "step_2": "The individual states: 'Natürlich Box A. Sichere 3000€ lehne ich nicht ab, wenn ich in der Alternative im schlechtesten Fall gar nichts Gewinne und im besten Fall NUR 1000€ mehr bekomme.' This translates to: 'Of course, Box A. I cannot refuse the sure 3000€, especially when in the alternative I get nothing in the worst case and only 1000€ more in the best case.' The individual considers the certainty of 3000€ in A versus the risk in B, which involves a 20% chance of getting nothing and an 80% chance of getting 4000€. The individual emphasizes the safety of A and contrasts it with the risk of B, where the best-case gain is only 1000€ more than the worst-case (0€). The individual does not mention any calculation of aspiration levels, differences from a mean, or probabilities of positive differences. The justification is based on risk aversion and preference for certainty, not on the aspiration level or the distribution of positive deviations from a mean. The deliberation process centers on the certainty and the limited upside of B, not on the mean outcome or differences from a mean.",
  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — the aspiration level (2000€ for B, 3000€ for A), the positive differences (2000€ in B with 80% probability, 0 in A), and the preference for higher probability of positive differences — is not considered or mentioned in the verbal report. The individual does not refer to any mean outcome or deviations from a mean. Instead, the justification is based on the sure gain and the limited upside of B, reflecting a risk-averse preference for certainty, not an aspiration-level-based evaluation. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason involving aspiration level and probability of positive differences. The reasoning process is inconsistent with the rule of the decision reason. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
